 "not_done": {
  "LibreOffice export filter without lossless images": "page_lines identical on y06 and the render ~20% faster there, but the JSON filter syntax needs LibreOffice >= 7.4 and a tester's older install would fail every render",
  "measure fewer pages per round": "the measurement aligns every source line with every rendered line; reusing a page's lines needs proof the rendered page is unchanged, and LibreOffice renumbers font subsets document-wide",
  "per-page page_lines in a process pool": "identical by construction and ~3x on 4 cores, but spawn on Windows/macOS re-runs an unguarded user script and nests under the sweep's own pool; would need opt-in",
  "re-serialise only what changed between rounds": "the writer carries cross-page state (sections, page breaks, bookmarks, note numbering, header parts); a partial rewrite could not be shown identical",
  "render only the changed range": "LibreOffice converts whole documents",
  "reuse the parse's characters for the source's page lines": "about 40% of the round-0 source read (3s on y13, 10s on y06); needs _page_chars split into its read and finish stages in parse_pdfium"
 },
